  "openDesignRulings": [
    "Advanced additional Pacts remain conceptually available but are not unlocked by current native progression; defer eligibility, level, cost, maximum, and renegotiation mechanics",
    "Invocation selection counts and budget compared with selected Pacts",
    "Which Patron abilities are granted at level 1 versus later advancement",
    "Native Eldritch Blast grant and improvements",
    "How historical at-will and modern slot-based abilities coexist",
    "Fiend feature edition reconciliation and repeatability/resource costs",
    "Pact break effects and Invocation restoration/transfer details: preserve prior acquisitions and model Pact affiliation; decide timing, refund/replacement, ownership migration, and legal restoration costs later.",
    "Invocation Pact/Patron requirements and Pact Patron requirements are supported; individual option restrictions are deferred to each option reconciliation. Do not impose blanket restrictions or assume waived prerequisites on transfer.",
    "Per-Pact Patron willingness can be constrained by specific setting or inherited terms; determine detailed acceptance/negotiation UX and secret-Patron adjudication later without imposing universal live negotiation.",
    "Level-5 Pact upgrades for Blade, Chain, Tome are owner-approved as a design; resolve Chain command/attack economy, Tome spell interaction, Thirsting Blade replacement and any post-level-5 progression before native activation.",
    "Resolve source-faithful base mechanics, the three Talisman-bound Invocations, and Pact-level progression for Talisman; do not silently give it the Blade/Chain/Tome Deepened Pact milestone.",
    "Resolve Star Chain as an independent Seeker-restricted UA Pact versus Tome overlap; playable Fiend+Star Chain is source-ineligible pending explicit approved alternative Patron qualification. Design its level-5 and later Pact progression separately."
  ],
